{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:61329dc1578276063fe3202a32f1e26f7ac62ffd90affde319e7611d6c901912","title":"Can realistic anomaly-free brane sectors be built without destabilizing closed fields needed for anomaly-canceling axions? Can explicit geometries, twisted-sector alternatives, or brane networks realize the effective constructions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:610a2f610a490ff9949bdebdffaff8238931239a968cebf16e43be7ca3be5e67","title":"Can gaugino-condensation stabilization of the dilaton coexist with radion stabilization by enhanced-symmetry momentum/winding strings, without their combined dynamics destabilizing either modulus? The paper presents a preliminary answer under simplifying approximations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6191e4e1ae33b5c8d874f2d996c2553616c76c297921ec2275216d5c58a12646","title":"How do vector field perturbations generate statistically anisotropic primordial curvature perturbations, and what spectra, bispectra and model constraints follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61dd62533816ba26dbafe0863cc2686a06133c7d8676beeb10cf1c57f61c689a","title":"Does the effective four-dimensional supergravity of stabilized K3 × T²/Z₂ compactifications admit slow-roll D3 motion, and how do bulk-modulus dynamics and the choice of uplifting affect its existence, tuning, and predictions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61361651de21b4ad525bbed123aef27f493286d11b1c7237e1c1c296b136fb0d","title":"Can the Kerr/CFT argument be extended to general four-dimensional extremal Kerr-Newman-AdS-dS black holes, reproducing their entropy through a chiral CFT, and can a regular alternative description be supplied when angular momentum vanishes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:616694ac90bab887f374a791ef7e411a6698e811965e7878fdd4f48dd706fc9b","title":"How can globally defined fermion/scalar wavefunctions and Yukawa overlaps be constructed for toroidal magnetized branes with oblique, mutually noncommuting flux matrices, including mixed eigenvalue signatures that exclude the familiar positive-chirality basis?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:612aa38b2da288a01d6e471e75d62c230783ce706e4bf83b972d8d665d0df828","title":"How can the measured cosmological constant remain stable under higher-loop corrections and changes of effective description? The lectures distinguish achieving radiative stability from predicting its numerical value.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61a3094b403d49cef56b084faadc5ba7c3e2bf5a691e50e86084348d2377f7d0","title":"Can flux-induced winding of complex-structure axions support controlled transplanckian natural inflation, while avoiding proposed instanton obstructions and remaining compatible with the mild axionic weak gravity conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61ce0ba2f2db04d28e2a5f4fd1b5ef8afa0aeaa2637b71d194727489a3b08c97","title":"How are negative branes and supergroup gauge theories connected to timelike compactification, dynamical spacetime-signature change and holographic emergence of time? Can protected calculations and dualities supply evidence for their nonperturbative existence?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:617119be7fe370fd838b7c471967f8619be8d649e41a22d8827d1fef0caa92cb","title":"Can a dark-energy scalar satisfy the negative-curvature branch while remaining observationally close to a cosmological constant? The example varies a hilltop height and tachyonic curvature, with its initial displacement controlling the amount of rolling.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:618c7476e9bd17d716b6730a0c83a5b14174deb00690e4bdd359630f74f131ed","title":"How do six- and eight-derivative gravitational EFT operators change Kerr thermodynamics at first order, can those changes be obtained without the corrected metric, and when do entropy corrections have definite signs?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61f6ace0f0b72c9797cd1be3b7acef5ec5d1246ed7ff2df6eaeac464f4bf10c2","title":"Can rescaling the higher-dimensional Gauss-Bonnet coupling by 1/(D−4), followed by a continuous D→4 limit, define modified four-dimensional gravity while retaining covariance, second-order dynamics, and only massless graviton polarizations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61491dad8c6cc74a5a02a539a3563db400aec227a4ef0dacd942f91d0b091d04","title":"Can signs of local inflaton effective interactions reveal the spins of particles heavier than the inflationary Hubble scale, and can their primordial non-Gaussianity shapes be separated from leading derivative interactions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0043"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61c0ded7baa5a9b0ddb5b4b477b6cb94eb0bd7b7ff33cf43e354771edd41cda7","title":"Which classical emergent-string trajectories survive quantum geometry, and can dilaton co-scaling prevent KK dominance in four-dimensional Type IIA?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61d9180c493feca279e8041eb4cdb977737e2a27d68a8e8fd866e8952b96dc66","title":"What string and effective dimension arise when an Abelian-surface fiber shrinks at finite Calabi–Yau volume? The wrapped M5 is identified with a Type II string; equal elliptic-area scalings define the genuine product-fiber Type T4 limit.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6118978b42fcf9a31011c264d7f44b591d31cddb91920cdfe5cbd6440eae0fda","title":"Does a compactification failing the unfluxed instanton screen remain correction-free after worldvolume flux and tadpole-required D3-branes are included?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0050"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6103cb74e7b301b20c797c1f72975546f40d5667af18a5b55c20e166352cbd85","title":"The setting supplies a nonlinear effective description of one massive and one massless gravitating spin-two field. Coupling matter to one metric fixes which cosmic time, stress tensor, and observable Hubble parameter enter the subsequent calculation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6118d7e96a4f864fc3e782183eb3e43d7a4be73f346ab0d364dfb0f008a67775","title":"How does a dark-matter interaction modify the expansion driven by a canonical scalar? Normalizing the interaction to unity today permits an effective phantom history without introducing a phantom scalar kinetic term.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61cc1a02b4b31ec8b0107932539c6f5abdb8f88f0a268e4589bba5535a61ffb8","title":"Could percent-level constraints on the dark-energy equation of state distinguish a modified-cosmology quintessence model from w=-1? The paper names several surveys and instruments as motivation for exploring that possibility.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6131a6c0aa4375fe3b59d41504466f7b76de87a8815953a9c3ec2646e852962b","title":"How can the conjectural Festina Lente bound be sharpened and extended to higher dimensions, scalar-dependent couplings and charged towers, and what conditional consequences follow for particle physics, dimensional reduction and antibrane uplifting?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61c29eda113cf5a5068348600acbbb1474571d5825e56057fe9f27e4e1c6e4c5","title":"How readily can sustained rapid-turn inflation arise in supergravity, and what do its turning rate, field-space curvature and Hessian spectrum imply for the multifield η-problem and de Sitter swampland conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:61cdec6cb0f83771dd84087399e8708a0073360b7a20701a80922e3072b0a0ab","title":"How can geometry, heterotic line-bundle consistency conditions and chiral spectra be computed for arbitrary local triangulations, and which conditions permit every triangulation simultaneously?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6128f5c0309b4b7e44c05793066368ccda3f1bf52837fccd9bb2d340f508209d","title":"How does topology affect the largest protected gap when the number of moduli can vary widely? Eight-supercharge Calabi–Yau compactifications provide a much larger set of theories than the higher-supersymmetry examples.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-quest